# Text is checked out with LF everywhere, Windows too: the licence notices
# are built into the binaries and compared with what xtask generates, and
# a test or build that reads a checked-out file should see the same bytes
# on every platform. rc.exe and the manifest read LF as well.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cargo-about copies crates' licence files as they are, and a few end their
# lines in CRLF; `cargo xtask licenses --check` compares them byte for byte
crates/core/licenses/THIRD-PARTY-CRATES.txt -text

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.webp binary
*.webm binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.tgs binary
